{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CfcTJw49xhjWvnLsMbSjZ", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "signature": ""}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 7611, "cache_read_input_tokens": 16975, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 7611}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "d95d5071-68c5-4232-900e-d7f21c2e3487", "uuid": "a45c4bc1-583d-4003-bd6f-16de586cf3af", "timestamp": "2026-10-02T00:21:14.115Z", "request_id": "req_011CfcTJvhZovm4N1M21PUbq", "thinking_duration_ms": 87}
{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CfcTJw49xhjWvnLsMbSjZ", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "**Lists can be changed after you create them, and tuples can't.** That one difference explains most of how they're used.\n\n| | List | Tuple |\n|---|---|---|\n| Syntax | `[1, 2, 3]` | `(1, 2, 3)` or `1, 2, 3` |\n| Mutable? | Yes: you can add, remove and replace items | No: fixed once created |\n| Methods | Many (`append`, `extend`, `insert`, `remove`, `pop`, `sort`, `reverse`, \u2026) | Only `count` and `index` |\n| Hashable? | No | Yes, if all its elements are hashable |\n| Use as dict key / set member | \u274c | \u2705 |\n| Memory / speed | Slightly larger and slower | Slightly smaller, faster to create |\n| Typical use | A collection of similar items that changes in size | A fixed record of related values |\n\n**Mutability**\n```python\nnums = [1, 2, 3]\nnums[0] = 10        # fine\nnums.append(4)      # fine\n\npoint = (1, 2)\npoint[0] = 10       # TypeError: 'tuple' object does not support item assignment\n```\n\n**Hashability** (dict keys and sets)\n```python\nlocations = {(40.7, -74.0): \"NYC\"}   # tuple key works\nlocations = {[40.7, -74.0]: \"NYC\"}   # TypeError: unhashable type: 'list'\n```\n\n**Things to watch out for:**\n- A one-element tuple needs a trailing comma: `(5,)` is a tuple, but `(5)` is just the integer `5`.\n- A tuple is only \"shallowly\" immutable. If it holds a mutable object, that object can still change:\n  ```python\n  t = ([1, 2], 3)\n  t[0].append(99)   # works \u2192 ([1, 2, 99], 3)\n  ```\n  A tuple like this also can't be hashed, because the list inside it can't be.\n\n**Convention:** Use a **list** for a collection of the same kind of item that may grow or shrink, like a list of user IDs. Use a **tuple** for a fixed group of values where each position means something, like `(x, y)`, `(name, age)` or a function returning several values (`return total, count`). If a tuple has many fields, `collections.namedtuple` or `typing.NamedTuple` let you access them by name."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 7611, "cache_read_input_tokens": 16975, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 7611}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "d95d5071-68c5-4232-900e-d7f21c2e3487", "uuid": "92975a69-b6de-417a-b819-76f8e232ea82", "timestamp": "2026-10-02T00:21:20.841Z", "request_id": "req_011CfcTJvhZovm4N1M21PUbq"}
